        "asr_text": "Used well, these settings can help fresh produce keep its quality longer, but the right choice is not simply fruit here, vegetables there. Fresh food can lose quality in different ways. Some foods release a gas as they ripen. That gas can make nearby produce ripen too quickly. Other foods lose water quickly and begin to wilt. So the useful question is not only, is this a fruit or a vegetable? It is also, what problem am I trying to prevent?",
