        "status": "OK",
        "asr_text": "There is one important boundary: Choosing low or high humidity only matters after you decide that the food belongs in the refrigerator. Tomatoes and bananas are recommended for counter storage rather than refrigeration, so they should not go in the low-humidity drawer simply because they release ripening gas. Potatoes, sweet potatoes, onions, and garlic do not need refrigeration; they are recommended for a cool, dry environment. That is not exactly the same as keeping them on the counter with tomatoes and bananas. The larger lesson is simple: First, choose the right storage place, then choose the right drawer setting.",
